This package installs the modern neotrickle implementation under the
familiar command names trickle and trickled.

It does NOT provide the classic trickle command-line interface,
configuration format (/etc/trickled.conf), or wire protocol.  Scripts
using classic flags or bare KB/s rates must be migrated.  Examples and
migration guidance are installed under /usr/share/doc/trickle/.

Configuration examples are documentation only.  Copy the files you need
to /etc/ntrickle/ and edit them:

  install -d /etc/ntrickle
  cp /usr/share/doc/trickle/examples/ntrickled.example.toml \
     /etc/ntrickle/ntrickled.toml

The ntrickled.service unit is installed but intentionally not enabled or
started by the package.  Enable it explicitly after reviewing the
configuration:

  systemctl enable --now ntrickled.service

The daemon's singleton lock file is intentionally retained after exit.
Do not add an ExecStartPre that deletes sockets or lock files; the daemon
removes only stale Unix sockets after acquiring its lock.  See
docs/daemon.md for details.

Rootless users can run standalone mode without root:

  trickle -m standalone -d 10M -- wget URL

or run a private per-user daemon:

  trickled --user
